Drop the numba stack from the numba extra

The `cuNN-dx` extras pull in `nvmath-python[numba]`, which installs numba-cuda
(unused by the numba-cuda-mlir backend) and a released numba-cuda-mlir that
would shadow the wheel built by this CI run. Reduce the extra to cffi, which the
numba-cuda-mlir device modules import; everything else in it exists only to
support numba-cuda.

numba and llvmlite go too: numba ships its own `numba/cuda` shim, so leaving it
installed would matter to nvmath's backend probe. 0001-disable-numba-cuda-backend.patch
removes that probe, which is also what makes a numba-free environment importable
at all.

This keeps `pip install <checkout>[cuNN-dx]` as the single install command, so
the rest of the dx dependency set stays in sync with upstream.

Context is kept to one line, but the removed lines carry version specifiers, so
this patch needs a refresh whenever upstream bumps either pin.
Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -117,7 +117,2 @@ numba = [
     "cffi",
-    "llvmlite",
-    # numba-cuda defines version restriction
-    "numba",
-    "numba-cuda >=0.28.1, <1",
-    "numba-cuda-mlir >=0.4.1, <1; python_version >= '3.11'",
 ]
